# PC Builder Rules

- PC Builder is a dedicated domain subsystem.
- Compatibility logic must not be buried inside React components.
- Keep compatibility rules data-driven and testable.
- Validate compatibility server-side when backend is available.
- Do not load the entire product database into the client.
- Support component selection, replacement, removal, totals, stock, warnings, save/share, and add-to-cart.
- Compatibility may include CPU socket, motherboard/RAM, form factor, storage interface, PSU requirements, GPU/case clearance, and other supported data.
- Never claim compatibility when the required data is unavailable; show an appropriate unknown state.
- Read `docs/PC_BUILDER.md` before major PC Builder work.
